(2100600, 281320, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Winding Road is a prefect shot for the Road challenge.  I think the simplicity of the shot is the most appealing.  The shot personally makes me feel like traveler on vacation who has finally reached the bed and breakfast that we have been traveling towards. <br/> <br/>I like the snow and the clean lines in the shot.  The composition is excellent.  The road is prefect clear and takes us somewhere.  The only thing I would have tried in the shot was maybe possibly moving the shot over so that the inn or house is on the left side more so the house is on the first third of the shot.  I really do like the shot and think the score is pretty decent and the Top 20 is not bad at all.  Excellent work.</td>', '*Critique Club* Winding Road is a prefect shot for the Road challenge.  I think the simplicity of the shot is the most appealing.  The shot personally makes me feel like traveler on vacation who has finally reached the bed and breakfast that we have been traveling towards.  I like the snow and the clean lines in the shot.  The composition is excellent.  The road is prefect clear and takes us somewhere.  The only thing I would have tried in the shot was maybe possibly moving the shot over so that the inn or house is on the left side more so the house is on the first third of the shot.  I really do like the shot and think the score is pretty decent and the Top 20 is not bad at all.  Excellent work.', '2006-01-30 01:41:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2100628, 280927, 45166, '<td valign="top">exxcellent choice of location.....gr8 work!!</td>', 'exxcellent choice of location.....gr8 work!!', '2006-01-30 01:46:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2100654, 282948, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Road of Ice is a good fit into the Road challenge.  I personally think night shot are some of the most challenging and most rewarding.  The glow from the lights onto the road really enhances the subject.  The trees also add to the effect of the light because the are so dark and add a level of depth to the shot.  I would be curious to see a tighter crop on the left hand side to take out at least the small couple of street signs.  I was looking at your score and placement which really aren''t too bad, but I think it would have been higher like agenkin said.  I think a lot of us (most of us) don''t see it but something just doesn''t seem quite right.  I really would be curious to see the shot flipped, I think it would have given the shot a nice classic winter night shot.</td>', '*Critique Club* Road of Ice is a good fit into the Road challenge.  I personally think night shot are some of the most challenging and most rewarding.  The glow from the lights onto the road really enhances the subject.  The trees also add to the effect of the light because the are so dark and add a level of depth to the shot.  I would be curious to see a tighter crop on the left hand side to take out at least the small couple of street signs.  I was looking at your score and placement which really aren''t too bad, but I think it would have been higher like agenkin said.  I think a lot of us (most of us) don''t see it but something just doesn''t seem quite right.  I really would be curious to see the shot flipped, I think it would have given the shot a nice classic winter night shot.', '2006-01-30 01:54:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2100734, 282368, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>By the road is a nice interpertation of the Road challenge.  I think voters have a pretty good idea of what they are looking for when they are voting and rarely to do you see a picture do extremely well when it doesn''t fit a certain idea.  I think you had great out of the box idea for the challenge.  The picture itself is nicely taken the positioning and cropping are just right.  I like the you included the shadow down fast his feet.  Also black and white is a prefect choice for this piece to bring out the subject.  Did you stage this shot? Personally I am curious because for some reason to me it feels staged, it didn''t take away from the way I voted but I was curious.  Great use of the light you had.  The shadows are one of the best pieces in this shot.  I am glad you chose to enter this into the challenge it really does fit and show a part of society that we often choose to look away from.  Good work</td>', '*Critique Club* By the road is a nice interpertation of the Road challenge.  I think voters have a pretty good idea of what they are looking for when they are voting and rarely to do you see a picture do extremely well when it doesn''t fit a certain idea.  I think you had great out of the box idea for the challenge.  The picture itself is nicely taken the positioning and cropping are just right.  I like the you included the shadow down fast his feet.  Also black and white is a prefect choice for this piece to bring out the subject.  Did you stage this shot? Personally I am curious because for some reason to me it feels staged, it didn''t take away from the way I voted but I was curious.  Great use of the light you had.  The shadows are one of the best pieces in this shot.  I am glad you chose to enter this into the challenge it really does fit and show a part of society that we often choose to look away from.  Good work', '2006-01-30 02:14:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2101460, 282948, 15711, '<td valign="top">I like this very much. The round glow of the lights amidst the black of the night sky is appealing. I appreciate the icy roads too, as they happen infrequently here, but when they do, the town shuts down and it''s very lonely outside - just as this depicts. This is very reminiscent of a Brassai photograph. If you''re not familiar with his work, look it up.</td>', 'I like this very much. The round glow of the lights amidst the black of the night sky is appealing. I appreciate the icy roads too, as they happen infrequently here, but when they do, the town shuts down and it''s very lonely outside - just as this depicts. This is very reminiscent of a Brassai photograph. If you''re not familiar with his work, look it up.', '2006-01-30 09:25:12.000000', NULL, 0),
