(2827167, 282449, 43463, '<td valign="top">My first reactions to viewing this image where "Wow" and "with all the crazy drivers down here in S. Florida this photog has got to be a brave &amp; crazy man":-) This is a very stunning image! Within your ''widescreen'' composition I absolutely love how you included the railings on the bridge   that along with the centered yellow dividing line just leads the eye directly up to the full moon seen off in the distance. The road, the railings and the yellow dividing line act like a runway that we travel down at high speed to then launch onwards and upwards off the ramp to that far distant moon. Love the title which is a direct reference to the Honeymooners. The show was before my time, but I have seen some of the famous snippets so I truly hear Gleason''s character sputtering "Straight to the moon, Alice! Straight to the moon!":-)</td>', 'My first reactions to viewing this image where "Wow" and "with all the crazy drivers down here in S. Florida this photog has got to be a brave & crazy man":-) This is a very stunning image! Within your ''widescreen'' composition I absolutely love how you included the railings on the bridge   that along with the centered yellow dividing line just leads the eye directly up to the full moon seen off in the distance. The road, the railings and the yellow dividing line act like a runway that we travel down at high speed to then launch onwards and upwards off the ramp to that far distant moon. Love the title which is a direct reference to the Honeymooners. The show was before my time, but I have seen some of the famous snippets so I truly hear Gleason''s character sputtering "Straight to the moon, Alice! Straight to the moon!":-)', '2006-09-12 10:40:30.000000', NULL, 0),
